-- Adds the first UPSC CSAT (Civil Services Aptitude Test) content to the site, closing the
-- biggest content gap found while continuing the UPSC-centric buildout (after the Indian Polity
-- sectional papers, see generate_upsc_polity_sectional_papers_2026_10_25.sql): CSAT is a
-- mandatory qualifying Prelims paper, and before this there wasn't a single UPSC-tagged paper for
-- it, despite Geography, Science & Tech, International Relations and Economy each already having
-- at least one live paper.
--
-- Unlike the Polity buildout, there was no dormant source bank to pull from for CSAT -- this
-- content was written from scratch. To keep that safe for an exam-prep site, generation was
-- deliberately split by how verifiable each question type is:
--   - Quantitative Aptitude (91 Qs: Percentages, Profit & Loss, SI/CI, Averages, Ratio &
--     Proportion, Time & Work, Time-Speed-Distance, Number Series, BODMAS) -- every correct
--     answer and every wrong-option distractor was COMPUTED by a Python script (not typed from
--     memory), so arithmetic correctness is guaranteed rather than asserted.
--   - Logical Reasoning (35 Qs: Coding-Decoding, Letter Series, Direction Sense, Blood
--     Relations, Syllogism, Classification, Analogy, Seating Arrangement) -- mechanical sub-types
--     (coding-decoding shifts, direction-sense vector sums) were also computed in code; the two
--     seating-arrangement puzzles were brute-force verified against all 4!/5! permutations to
--     confirm each has a unique, logically consistent solution (an earlier draft of the circular
--     seating puzzle turned out to have NO valid solution and was caught and rewritten this way).
--   - Data Interpretation & Basic Numeracy (12 Qs) -- built from two small constructed tables,
--     with every question's answer (sums, % growth, ratios, highest-value lookups) derived
--     directly from those table values in code.
--
-- Kannada fields (q_kn/options_kn/exp_kn) are deliberately left out of every question rather than
-- filled with duplicated English text -- the real exam engine already falls back to English when
-- they're empty (`q.q_kn || q.q_en`, confirmed in js/10_omr_exam_engine.js and
-- js/11b_practice_mistakes_topic_builder.js), so omitting them is correct, not incomplete; filling
-- them with English would have falsely presented untranslated text as Kannada.
--
-- Packaged as 2 free papers (continuing the "free to build traffic" pricing decision from the
-- Polity buildout), dual-tagged category upsc_cse + extra_categories kpsc_kas (KPSC KAS has an
-- analogous qualifying General Aptitude paper, per the "Aptitude and Reasoning PYQ Analysis- KAS"
-- and "Paper 2- Aptitude Analysis" PDFs already in pdf_vault).
--
-- Post-insert verification (run against the live rows, not just the source script): both papers'
-- question_count matches jsonb_array_length exactly (91, 47); every question has exactly 4
-- options with all 4 distinct; every `correct` index is within 0-3; all 138 question ids are
-- distinct; and a spot-check of first/middle/last questions in each paper against the known
-- source text matched exactly (first/last confirmed via SELECT, not re-trusted from the INSERT
-- text alone).

